+# Experimental Microsoft PC port: engine build 7445165
+
+## September 19 startup warning correction
+
+Native commit `220a4a468bf5496bdd2a80251718acda0cc13d7f` adds an exact-name optional-mapping policy before the existing symbol mapper runs. `App::UpdatePaths` may be missing only when CustomProfile is empty; `ui::DataContextProvider::ExecuteCommandQueues` has no callback consumer in this revision. Critical declarations override the new policy. Missing pointers stay null and explicit capability warnings remain logged. The global failure aggregation and error-dialog code are unchanged.
+
+`Test-OptionalMappings.cpp` supplies 12 compile-time cases covering requested features, critical precedence, unrelated mappings and near matches. Actual isolated Xbox startup on September 19 reached the main menu with v33 loaded and no startup popup. Client initialization and Lua VM reset are in `Logs/ScriptExtender/Extender Runtime 2026-09-19 09-58-18.log`; `EarlyRuntime-11900.log` retains the capability warnings. This targeted test did not load a campaign. All user packages/orders were restored byte-for-byte.
+
+DLL SHA-256: `846057960E4D9E7544E87E15D58948BBC4F7E2BA08153007F7D2C0F1C2DFC85D`. The September 15 full Lua/Osiris/save/reload verification below describes the earlier native build; it is retained as historical evidence.
+
+Upstream: Norbyte/bg3se commit `77e9072f1092eda7c657352ed21040f1664f3ee5` (2026-09-13). Local branch: `local/microsoft-7445165-investigation`.
+
+**Status: build 12 passed client/server Lua, Osiris callbacks and queries, gameplay, new modded save, normal quit/restart and reload.** MCM settings and callbacks also have runtime proof. The original BG3 executable remains unchanged. See the workspace VerificationLedger.json for per-binary evidence and remaining limits.
+
+## Exact target and version policy
+
+Package: `LarianStudiosGamesLtd.baldurssgate3_1.8.907.0_x64__551z37b1dechw`. Executable: `C:\XboxGames\Baldur's Gate 3\Content\bg3.exe`, x64 DX11. Fixed resource version: 4.1.1.39597; SpecialBuild and main-menu build: 7445165.
+
+The official v32 DWrite proxy has already executed in this process, but online release selection rejects the fixed resource version. The prepared test uses the upstream loader's DebugLoadSE development option to load the local BG3ScriptExtender.dll. The runtime still requires the exact package, fixed version, SpecialBuild string and x64 PE header. No false Steam version, entitlement change, executable substitution or alternative injection mechanism is involved.
+
+## Source changes
+
+All engine changes require `BG3SE_MICROSOFT_7445165`. Without it, upstream ABI and version checks remain.
+
+| Source | Change and evidence |
+|---|---|
+| BuildIdentity.h; GameHooks/DataLibraries.h/.cpp | Exact package/build validation and safer resource-allocation failure paths. Unknown builds rejected. |
+| DataLibrariesBG3Game.cpp; Extender/Client/IMGUI/IMGUI.cpp | Identify this exact Microsoft bg3.exe as DX11; live modules and game window confirm it. |
+| GameDefinitions/FileReader.h | Two 32-bit handles match live constructor/destructor instructions. Static assertions: Buffer 0x28, Type 0x80, FileObject 0x88, size 0x90. |
+| GameDefinitions/Symbols.h; DataLibraries.cpp | Adapt Microsoft's one-pointer free wrapper. Require its internal allocator getter to equal the independently mapped allocation getter; mismatch is a critical initialization failure. |
+| Build-MicrosoftMappings.ps1 and generated BinaryMappingsMicrosoft7445165.xml | Five earlier candidate replacements, allocator sequence, App constructor/instance register change, statistics loader short branch. String guards and critical checks retained. |
+| BG3Extender.rc | Embed Microsoft mappings only in opt-in build; original UTF-16 encoding retained. |
+| Directory.Build.targets | Optional MSBuild define; no upstream post-build deployment. |
+| Generate-CMake.py; Build-Microsoft.ps1 | Portable MSVC build derives source lists, includes, release defines and libraries from upstream projects. Generates enums, property maps, protobuf code and Lua bundle. No deployment. |
+
+## Evidence and remaining validation
+
+The read-only live audit resolved all 16 top-level critical mappings plus chained client DoWork, with literal guards and target references checked. Multiple candidate call sites are accepted only if target tuples agree. This is binding evidence, not runtime proof.
+
+The allocator mapping uses independently checked free-wrapper/allocation body guards. The App creation sequence uses R14 instead of R12, retaining its Creating App string guard. StatsShared retains the first 111 upstream bytes and changes the last near JBE to short JBE. Independent lookup through the live fixed-string pool returned PassiveData, satisfying its original guard. The runtime uses patterns, not hardcoded observed RVAs.
+
+Evidence in the parent workspace Logs directory: BG3SE-CriticalReferenceAudit.json, BG3SE-AllocatorContracts.json, BG3SE-AppCreation.json, BG3SE-StatsSharedFunction.json, BG3SE-StatsSharedStringGuard.json, BG3SE-LivePackageIdentity.json and BG3SE-SecondaryPatternAudit.json.
+
+Two noncritical mappings remain unresolved: App::UpdatePaths (custom profile relocation) and ui::DataContextProvider::ExecuteCommandQueues (no active callback consumer found). A startup warning still reports these. No executable version or allocator safety check is disabled to force initialization.
+
+## Portable build
+
+Administrator-based Visual Studio installation did not complete. Microsoft compiler/SDK packages were instead extracted inside the workspace without Windows Installer actions or global security changes:
+
+- MSVC directory 14.51.36231; compiler 19.51.36257.
+- Windows SDK 10.0.26100.0.
+- CMake 4.4.3; Ninja 1.13.2; workspace Python.
+- Upstream dependency revisions: Logs/BG3SE-BuildDependencies.json.
+
+Source/portable-msvc-upstream.py preserves mmozeiko's original downloader. Source/portable-msvc-local.py restricts paths to the workspace, checks archive destinations and Microsoft manifest hashes, extracts SDK MSIs using LessMSI, and retains downloads/staging. It runs no MSI actions, recursive cleanup or system environment changes. Logs: PortableMSVC-retry.log and CMakeNinjaSources.json.
+
+Build with PowerShell 7:
+
+    & 'C:\BG3Build\Source\bg3se\MicrosoftCompatibility\Build-Microsoft.ps1' -Jobs 1
+
+Output: Build/BG3SE-Microsoft/BG3ScriptExtender.dll in the parent workspace. First build log: Logs/BG3SE-MicrosoftBuild-1.log. A successful compilation is not runtime verification.
+
+## Prepared runtime test and rollback
+
+Source/Deploy-ExperimentalSE.ps1 validates the package and official loader hash, then journals/backups the local DLL, proxy and two configuration files. It refuses deployment while BG3 runs. The development loader selects the exact local runtime. Crash uploads and network debuggers are disabled for tests.
+
+Source/SEProbe records client/server Lua startup, session/game-state events, a real LevelGameplayStarted Osiris event, and read-only host entity/stat queries. These executed in the disposable BG3SE Test campaign. The probe does not change story flags or characters.
+
+Restore-BG3-ModSetup.ps1 defaults to dry-run and includes the local runtime DLL in its allowed rollback files. The updated isolated fixture test passed. Changed/newer files and unrelated mods remain protected; live saves and Xbox cloud containers are never overwritten by this workflow.
+
+## Build and input-binding follow-up
+
+The first compilation was intentionally stopped to increase parallelism after closing BG3. The second reached the runtime code and stopped at MSVC C1128 in LuaSharedLibs.cpp. The portable generator now applies /bigobj to the four large Lua units identified by upstream project options; optimized release settings remain. Build continuation is logged in Logs/BG3SE-MicrosoftBuild-3.log. Protobuf generation now skips current outputs to avoid recompiling unrelated code after a small fix.
+
+The Microsoft binary omits keyboard_WhiteBoxing.json but retains keyboard_1.json and controller_WhiteBoxing.json. Both profile-loader functions independently reference input-manager global RVA 0x5BB1D00 and its input-scheme member at +0xF8. The replacement mapping is a unique instruction sequence guarded by the retained controller profile string; no fixed RVA is used at runtime. Evidence: Logs/BG3SE-InputProfileReferences.json, BG3SE-InputControllerFunction.json and BG3SE-InputAndUIPatterns.json. The data-context command-queue mapping remains unresolved; no source consumer currently attaches a callback to that hook.
+
+## Additional bindings audited 2026-09-15
+Six additional mappings were matched against the live Microsoft process, with one unique full-pattern match each (Logs/BG3SE-SixAdditionalBindings.json):
+- Nine-case stats-functor dispatcher uses RSI instead of R14 for the same original argument; all nine relative call targets retained.
+- DealDamage call site swaps RBX/RDI register allocation; stack sources and argument positions are unchanged.
+- DynamicStatsExpressionManager resolves the same global from three independent 1d4 expression call sites; literal guard retained.
+- StatusPrototype::Init now uses the TELEPORT_FALLING (ID 4) call site; live fixed-string lookup verified the guard and callee arguments.
+- InterruptPrototype::Init retains the 0x220 object stride and statistics-object argument; getter/callee disassembly inspected.
+- AiGrid FindPath/FindPathImmediate retain the same two-argument call chain; Microsoft uses a short conditional branch and different result register.
+These mappings resolved at runtime on build 8. This is not a claim of complete ABI coverage.
+
+### Damage event binding (15 September)
+Audited the actual Microsoft DealDamageFunctor::ApplyDamage function. The six arguments and hit-type/damage comparisons identify the call at RVA 0x32E3105 to the 913-byte StatsSystem damage-event function at 0x2F2D560. Stack temporaries moved by 0x10; the StatsSystem local moved to RBP+0x98. The revised full call-site pattern uniquely matches 0x32E30E5; no target offset is hardcoded. Evidence is in BG3SE-ApplyDamageFullAudit.json, BG3SE-ThrowDamageCallee.json, and BG3SE-ThrowDamageMapping.json under the work Logs directory.
+
